    "manage.help.gallery.source.errorCode": "An extra line such as SOURCE_NOT_FOUND, SOURCE_PERMISSION_DENIED or SOURCE_READ_FAILED is the latest scan run's technical error code. Read it together with both phrases above; it is not a Manifest error code.",
    "manage.help.gallery.manifest.title": "Manifest column", "manage.help.gallery.manifest.intro": "Manifest means the Gallery's .cosplay.json sidecar (for archives, a same-directory sidecar named after the archive). The list displays the last persisted inspection, not a fresh file read for every row. Source IN_SYNC and Manifest CLEAN are independent.",
    "manage.help.gallery.manifest.UNCHECKED": "No Manifest inspection result has been recorded yet. This is unknown, not proof that a file is absent. Open the Gallery's Manifest tab or wait for enabled scheduled inspection.",
    "manage.help.gallery.manifest.STALE": "The Gallery metadata revision or source path changed since the recorded inspection. Recheck before deciding; STALE alone does not mean the file changed or is damaged.",
    "manage.help.gallery.manifest.NONE": "No sidecar and no established synchronization baseline. This is common before the first explicit Push and is not itself an error.",
    "manage.help.gallery.manifest.CLEAN": "At the last check, the tracked file hash and database revision matched the synchronization baseline. Later external changes still require a new check to be seen.",
    "manage.help.gallery.manifest.DB_DIRTY": "The database revision or tracked state changed after the last synchronization. Preview distinguishes a real sidecar-content change from a revision-only change; the latter need not rewrite the file.",
    "manage.help.gallery.manifest.FILE_DIRTY": "A valid sidecar changed outside CGM relative to its baseline, or a valid sidecar exists before the first baseline. Review it before overwriting or pulling.",
